joe_doufu wrote:
> Is Nethack available in languages other than English?  Is there, for
> example, a Chinese version?  I live in China and I think it would be
> fun to share the game with some of my friends and (university)
> students.  If not, how tough is it to implement a foreign-language
> version... does the source code use a language file that could be
> translated without having to modify the rest of the code, or would
> somebody really have to get their hands dirty?  I might have some
> volunteer translators in mind...

There are really a lot of message literals coded in the Nethack
source. Then there are huge amounts of object and monster tables
to be transliterated/translated. You may have noticed that Nethack
supports some basic grammar handling, so you'd have to implement
that in the code, too. Then all the quest data, quite some text,
that works with variables considering the respective grammar rules.
Then you need to translate all the rumors. To complete the task
you surely want to have a hand on the ingame help file information.
And last but not least the guidebook.

Sometimes I get the feeling that Nethack consists solely on data
for all the messages and no control code at all. ;-)

It might be easier to play Nethack as it is. :-)

But if you want to try... - good luck!

